age Trend Plot**\\n   - Shows batting or bowling average over time  \\n   - Identifies improvement or decline  \\n\\n5. **Runs Distribution Chart**\\n   - Shows frequency of scores (0–10, 50+, etc.)  \\n   - Measures consistency  \\n\\n6. **Wickets-Runs Scatter Plot**\\n   - Compare wickets vs runs conceded  \\n   - Identify best bowler  \\n\\n7. **Player Comparison Graphs**\\n   - Compare multiple players visually  \\n   - Compare runs, wickets, averages  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Benefits of Visualization\\n\\n- Easy to understand performance  \\n- Identifies trends quickly  \\n- Helps compare players  \\n- Improves decision making  \\n- Makes analysis visually clear  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Conclusion\\nVisualization techniques in cricketr use **graphs, plots, and charts** to analyze batting and bowling performance, making cricket data **easy to interpret and compare**.\",{},{\"_135\":243,\"_142\":288,\"_32\":289,\"_145\":290,\"_147\":148,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":291,\"_154\":155},\"fa58f9a7-820f-452c-84e3-c0bee50214ae\",[225],{\"_197\":240,\"_152\":296},1775892712.694,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":295},{\"_231\":292,\"_233\":293,\"_170\":252,\"_235\":-5,\"_174\":253,\"_165\":49,\"_181\":10,\"_177\":14},[],{\"_236\":294},[],[173],{},{\"_135\":286,\"_142\":300,\"_32\":301,\"_145\":302,\"_147\":148,\"_149\":26,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":303,\"_154\":155,\"_156\":157},\"6b4ba8dd-525d-41df-9dcf-516e0cc28408\",[243],{\"_197\":198,\"_152\":314},1775892663.249067,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":312},{\"_158\":304,\"_160\":26,\"_161\":305,\"_163\":306,\"_165\":49,\"_168\":307,\"_170\":308,\"_172\":173,\"_174\":309,\"_176\":49,\"_48\":49,\"_177\":26,\"_178\":298,\"_179\":310,\"_181\":10},{\"_28\":188,\"_189\":311},[],[],[],\"a473b8ba-49ff-4519-9740-e51aa2a68978\",\"aea3c2cb-7662-4f12-93f1-606ebc8a4e98\",341,[191],[313],\"### Q1 (f) — How to do analysis of bowlers with Wicket Frequency percentage and Wickets-Runs plot?\\n\\n### Meaning\\n- This analysis evaluates **bowler effectiveness**\\n- Uses **Wicket Frequency %** and **Wickets vs Runs plot**\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Wicket Frequency Percentage\\n\\n1. **Definition**\\n   - Measures how often a bowler takes wickets\\n\\n2. **Formula**\\n   - Wicket Frequency % = (Number of wickets ÷ Matches or overs) × 100  \\n\\n3. **Interpretation**\\n   - High value → bowler takes wickets regularly  \\n   - Low value → bowler struggles to take wickets  \\n\\n4. **Example**\\n   - Wickets = 10 in 5 matches  \\n   - Wicket Frequency % = (10/5) × 100 = 200%\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Wickets-Runs Plot\\n\\n5. **Plot Description**\\n   - X-axis → Runs conceded  \\n   - Y-axis → Wickets taken  \\n\\n6. **Interpretation**\\n   - High wickets \u0026 low runs → Best bowler  \\n   - Low wickets \u0026 high runs → Poor bowler  \\n   - High wickets \u0026 high runs → Aggressive but expensive  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Combined Analysis\\n\\n7. **Performance Evaluation**\\n   - High wicket frequency + low runs → Excellent  \\n   - High wicket frequency + high runs → Risky  \\n   - Low wicket frequency + low runs → Defensive bowler  \\n   - Low wicket frequency + high runs → Ineffective  \\n\\n---\\n\\n### Conclusion\\nWicket Frequency % shows **how often wickets are taken**, while Wickets-Runs plot shows **balance between wickets and runs**, helping evaluate bowler effectiveness.\",{},{\"_135\":298,\"_142\":318,\"_32\":319,\"_145\":320,\"_147\":148,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":321,\"_154\":155},\"a4c1a697-eb29-4e8e-b980-dbfcb7761875\",[286],{\"_197\":240,\"_152\":326},1775892655.353,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":325},{\"_231\":322,\"_233\":323,\"_170\":308,\"_235\":-5,\"_174\":309,\"_165\":49,\"_181\":10,\"_177\":14},[],{\"_236\":324},[],[173],{},{\"_135\":316,\"_142\":330,\"_32\":331,\"_145\":332,\"_147\":148,\"_149\":26,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":333,\"_154\":155,\"_156\":157},\"c481923c-37b6-4670-b7af-0ddaa45a50bf\",[298],{\"_197\":198,\"_152\":350},1775892618.512249,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":348},{\"_158\":334,\"_160\":26,\"_161\":335,\"_163\":336,\"_165\":49,\"_168\":337,\"_170\