aced, and time at crease**, helping estimate a batsman’s future scoring performance.\",{},{\"_135\":460,\"_142\":480,\"_32\":481,\"_145\":482,\"_147\":148,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":483,\"_154\":155},\"a69a9957-27ae-4eb7-a18d-6b1baf6ea20d\",[448],{\"_197\":240,\"_152\":488},1775891415.518,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":487},{\"_231\":484,\"_233\":485,\"_170\":470,\"_235\":-5,\"_174\":471,\"_165\":49,\"_181\":10,\"_177\":14},[],{\"_236\":486},[],[173],{},{\"_135\":478,\"_142\":492,\"_32\":493,\"_145\":494,\"_147\":148,\"_149\":26,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":495,\"_154\":155,\"_156\":157},\"f494e198-50f1-4635-9cc9-707af1636348\",[460],{\"_197\":198,\"_152\":512},1775891317.055639,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":510},{\"_158\":496,\"_160\":26,\"_161\":497,\"_163\":498,\"_165\":49,\"_168\":499,\"_170\":500,\"_172\":173,\"_174\":501,\"_176\":49,\"_48\":49,\"_177\":26,\"_178\":490,\"_179\":502,\"_181\":10},{\"_28\":188,\"_189\":509},[],[503],[],\"3ff2f0ba-86e0-4a10-b143-1a414aba994d\",\"a8a024ce-d364-407f-af36-7c759a987112\",343,{\"_256\":257,\"_258\":-5,\"_259\":504,\"_261\":505,\"_44\":506,\"_264\":507,\"_266\":267,\"_268\":267,\"_28\":269,\"_270\":267,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":151,\"_152\":-5,\"_274\":-5,\"_275\":508,\"_147\":277,\"_278\":-5,\"_279\":-5,\"_135\":-5},25,87,[],[],{\"_280\":281},[191],[511],\"### Q1 (c) — Explain how entity[\\\"software\\\",\\\"cricketr\\\",\\\"R cricket analytics package\\\"] can be used to compare players' performances over matches. (2025)\\n\\n### Meaning\\n- Player comparison means **evaluating performance of two or more players**\\n- cricketr helps compare **runs, wickets, averages and strike rates**\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Ways cricketr Compares Players\\n\\n1. **Runs Comparison**\\n   - Compare **total runs scored**\\n   - Identify better batsman\\n   - Useful for match performance comparison\\n\\n2. **Batting Average Comparison**\\n   - Compare **consistency of players**\\n   - Higher average → more reliable\\n\\n3. **Strike Rate Comparison**\\n   - Compare scoring speed\\n   - Helps identify aggressive batsman\\n\\n4. **Wickets Comparison**\\n   - Compare total wickets taken\\n   - Identify effective bowler\\n\\n5. **Economy Rate Comparison**\\n   - Compare runs conceded\\n   - Lower economy → better control\\n\\n6. **Match-wise Performance**\\n   - Compare performance across **multiple matches**\\n   - Identify consistency\\n\\n7. **Visualization Graphs**\\n   - Runs vs matches plot\\n   - Wickets vs matches plot\\n   - Average comparison charts\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Example\\n- Player A runs: 45, 67, 12, 89  \\n- Player B runs: 22, 40, 55, 60  \\n→ Player A higher peak, Player B more consistent\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Conclusion\\ncricketr compares players using **runs, averages, strike rates, wickets and graphs**, helping identify **better and more consistent performers across matches**.\",{},{\"_135\":490,\"_142\":516,\"_32\":517,\"_145\":518,\"_147\":148,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":519,\"_154\":155},\"dc70746f-9067-4ec5-820b-c128b12145a0\",[478],{\"_197\":240,\"_152\":524},1775891309.434,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":523},{\"_231\":520,\"_233\":521,\"_170\":500,\"_235\":-5,\"_174\":501,\"_165\":49,\"_181\":10,\"_177\":14},[],{\"_236\":522},[],[173],{},{\"_135\":514,\"_142\":528,\"_32\":529,\"_145\":530,\"_147\":148,\"_149\":26,\"_150\":151,\"_152\":531,\"_154\":155,\"_156\":157},\"7cf226f1-6eb5-48ef-a638-0d03a993613b\",[490],{\"_197\":198,\"_152\":542},1775891272.134593,{\"_192\":193,\"_194\":540},{\"_158\":532,\"_160\":26,\"_161\":533,\"_163\":534,\"_165\":49,\"_168\":535,\"_170\":536,\"_172\":173,\"_174\":537,\"_176\":49,\"_48\":49,\"_177\":26,\"_178\":526,\"_179\":538,\"_181\":10},{\"_28\":188,\"_189\":539},[],[],[],\"aad3c20e-7660-4335-a9a7-298c25ea65b6\",\"454fcb22-5d03-42ec-9a8b-79aad1c2de08\",386,[191],[541],\"### Q1 (c) — How to Check Bowler In-Form or Out-of-Form?\\n\\n### Meaning\\n- A bowler is **in-form** when taking **wickets regularly** and conceding **fewer runs**\\n- A bowler is **out-of-form** when taking **few wickets** and 